    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητῐόεις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆτις</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wise in counsel</i>,
			epith. of Zeus, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητίετα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				344
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				51
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				769
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάρμακα μητιόεντα</span>
			<i>wise</i>, i.e. <i>wellchosen, helpful</i> remedies, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.227
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δόλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aet.
					3.18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
